If a patient has a continuous-opioid-use and the continuous-opioid-use has a duration and the duration includes at least 1 week and the duration includes less than 1 month and a taper-schedule has a taper-interval and the taper-interval includes 2 days and the taper-schedule has a daily-opioid-dosage-reduction and the daily-opioid-dosage-reduction includes 20 percent and the taper-schedule is a gradual-taper then every clinician may use the taper-schedule for the patient.
